{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.KZLevelFromHeckeNormalisation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.KZLevelFromHeckeNormalisation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZLevelFromHeckeNormalisation.eigen_pair_of_product_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZLevelFromHeckeNormalisation.eigen_pair_of_product_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZLevelFromHeckeNormalisation.lean#L66-L86","doc":"The two signed solutions: `(a, b) = (q, −q⁻¹)` or `(−q, q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZLevelFromHeckeNormalisation.eigen_sq_of_product_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZLevelFromHeckeNormalisation.eigen_sq_of_product_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZLevelFromHeckeNormalisation.lean#L54-L64","doc":"If two eigenvalues have product `−1` and ratio `−q²`, they are `q, −q⁻¹` up to a common sign:\n`λ₂² = q⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KZLevelFromHeckeNormalisation.ratio_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KZLevelFromHeckeNormalisation.ratio_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KZLevelFromHeckeNormalisation.lean#L50-L52","doc":"Rescaling both eigenvalues by the same non-zero scalar leaves their ratio unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0}]}